    "review": "On November 29, 1970 at Club Agora in Columbus, the Dead delivered a tight early‑period set that still manages to excite listeners over six decades later. Highlights include an intense, pedal‑steel‑colored run through The Other One where Jerry’s lead is hot and forward, and a rollicking Good Lovin' that lifts the room despite the tape's fair fidelity. The band rides a solid groove through Truckin', classic country–rock numbers like Cumberland Blues, and closes with the familiar sing‑along of Not Fade Away/Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad. While the audience recording is a bit muddy and carries the usual 1970 hiss, it captures the crowd’s enthusiasm and provides an enjoyable snapshot of the Dead in their pre‑Mydland era.",
